## Results

Both runs started Linux `/init`, reached `retired=2,999,999,998`, stopped at
`budget_exhausted`, and passed exact nonce validation. The series scenario
outcome was `passed`; the automatic strict comparison was `matches=false`, exit
code 1, with unexplained `machine_observations` and
`ordered_uart_bytes` differences. No normalization was added by this slice.

| Run | RDTSC reads | PIT `0x61` reads | PIT `0x42` reads | PM reads | Halt idle ns | Virtual ns | Residual ns | Quanta | IRQ0 edges / delivered |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 0001 | 34,443,745 | 1 | 16,672 | 230 | 1,136,513 | 37,461,784,511 | 34,460,418,000 | 34,570,225 | 34,804 / 34,809 |
| 0002 | 34,450,132 | 1 | 16,672 | 230 | 1,769,420 | 37,468,804,418 | 34,466,805,000 | 34,576,373 | 34,811 / 34,816 |

Residual is `virtual_ns - retired - halt_idle_ns - pm_timer_reads × 1,000 ns`.
Each residual exactly equals `(rdtsc_reads + pit_0x61_reads +
pit_0x42_reads) × 1,000 ns`. PM and PIT counts match across runs; RDTSC differs
by 6,387 reads, which exactly accounts for the 6,387,000 ns residual delta.
The full `virtual_ns` delta is 7,019,907 ns: the remaining 632,907 ns equals
the difference in explicit halt idle. This accounting does not establish why
guest execution issued a different number of RDTSC instructions or spent a
different amount of time halted.

Both nonce lines were intact, but their order relative to the kernel printk
reversed: run 0001 emitted nonce before `[2.270895] Run /init as init process`;
run 0002 emitted `[2.270736] Run /init as init process` before nonce. The strict
machine comparison also retains differences in
`rdtsc_reads` (34,443,745/34,450,132), `cr3_changes` (26,618/26,617), and
`set_exit_detail` (`Run(InstructionBudgetExhausted)` /
`Run(StopRequested)`). These are observations, not declared benign. S5-07
remains blocked/unaccepted; do not normalize them without further evidence.

